   "text": {
    "L1": "India has mountains, deserts, plains and coasts. Each land has its own weather and features.",
    "L2": "A desert is a place with very little rain. Deserts can be hot, like the Thar, or cold, like Ladakh.",
    "L3": "So the idea that all deserts are hot is not true. Ladakh is a cold desert with snowy mountains.",
    "L4": "Mountains are colder higher up, so people wear thick woollens and grow crops that suit the cold.",
    "L5": "Plains are flat, with rivers and rich soil. Farming crops like wheat and rice is common there.",
    "L6": "Coasts are near the sea, with humid air. Many people fish, grow coconuts and eat rice and fish.",
    "L7": "People's clothes, food and work match their weather and land. That is why ways of living differ across India.",
    "L8": "Now use the clue about very little rain and freezing cold. Tap the region that is a cold desert."
   },
